The "Two-Factor Authentication" interface.

•	The interface is visually organized into three principal areas: the status area, the navigation/header area, and the content area:
o	Status Bar: Spanning the uppermost portion of the display from left to right:
	Time: Displays the local time as 4:24. Positioned to its right is the silent mode icon.
	Dynamic Island: The Dynamic Island is centered at the top of the display. A solid red circular indicator is visible toward its left side, consistent with the iOS screen-recording status indicator.
	Connectivity & Power: The Signal Strength icon displays two active black bars and two inactive gray bars, accompanied by the adjacent network label LTE. On the far right, the battery icon is partially filled, displaying the numeric charge level 44 centered within the housing.
•	Navigation & Header Bar: Establishing the user's hierarchical location within the iOS environment:
o	Back-Navigation: The upper-left margin displays a back-navigation link labeled "Back" accompanied by a directional chevron.
o	Primary Heading: Centrally aligned with the menu context, rendered in bold black typography:  "Two-Factor Authentication."
•	Interface Body: Positioned immediately below the navigation bar, the primary body content begins near the upper portion of the screen, presenting the  Two-Factor authentication management settings:
